                <pb facs="0087" n="17" sameAs="frus:frus1934v04/pg17"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.G Commercial Agreement/32: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gilbert</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-09-21T17:00:00-04:00">September 21, 1934—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>97. Your 259, September 21, 5 p.m. The Agreement was signed on behalf of United
                    States September 20. Every effort will be made to obtain favorable action by
                    Senate promptly after next session starts.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
